# Beyond &quot;Davis&quot;: Equality of Opportunity for Higher Education for Disabled Students under the Rehabilitation Act of 1973.

**Authors:** Cook, Timothy, Laski, Frank

## Abstract
Considers effects of section 504 (Title V) upon disabled applicants to, and students at, U.S. colleges and universities. Analyzes the Supreme Court's decision in &quot;Southeastern Community College v. Davis,&quot; focusing on postsecondary education provisions of DHEW enforcement regulations. Discusses policy ramifications regarding the implementation of provisions guaranteed in section 504. (Author/GC)

